Dusk OS was created by Virgil Dupras.

I was not entirely alone in creating it though. Some people wrote significant
parts of it:

Michael Schierl
  - Graphical grid [gr/grid]
  - Usermode Dusk
  - POSIX/SDL port
  - Oberon emulator [emul/oberon]
  - [app/ed] improvements
  - System Clipboard [text/clip]
  - Many Duskberon modules:
    - [oberon/clipboar]
    - [oberon/convertp]
    - [oberon/dumpfont]
    - [oberon/fontsubs]
    - [oberon/growfont]
    - [oberon/optimize]
    - [oberon/draw]
  - The posix/kbdconv utility

Arcade Wise
  - PC driver for CMOS real time clock [drv/pc/rtc]

Lucas Chaloyard
  - RISC-V assembler [asm/riscv]
  - RISC-V kernel [xcomp/riscv/kernel]

Bruno Franco
  - 11 rings of Dis(assembly) [doc/howto/asmrings]

Aaron Miller
  - Improvements to x86 assembler [asm/x86]
  - Improvements to PC bootloader [xcomp/i386/pc/mbr]
  - PBR bootloader [xcomp/i386/pc/pbr]
  - Allowing the PC kernel and [drv/pc/int13h] to do LBA accesses
  - MBR partition manager [io/part/mbr]

Ruben Lysens
  - RISC-V disassembler [asm/riscvd]
  - [asm/riscv] improvements

Drache
  - HAL improvements and optimizations across the board
  - [num/double] unit
  - Improve [lib/bit]
  - [num/xxhash] unit
  - Improve [hal/opq]
  - [num/chacha] unit
  - [gr/rdwr] improvements
  - Improve [lib/coop]
  - posix/time.c
  - Improve [hal/instr]

Other people have made smaller contributions and are listed below in order
of "appearance". To know the nature of those contributions, look
in the history of the git repository.

binarycat from flounder.online
Kartik K. Agaram
